## Component Implementation Details

### Smart Input Interface (Task 2)
```typescript
// Smart Company Input Component (from Story 2.2)
interface SmartInputProps {
  onSubmit: (input: OptimizedUserInput) => void;
  isGenerating: boolean;
  previousCompanies: string[];
}

interface OptimizedUserInput {
  companyName: string;
  companyUrl?: string;
  linkedinUrl?: string;
  additionalContext?: string;
  organizationFocus?: string;
  locationOfInterest?: string;
  priority: 'standard' | 'express';
  outputFormat: 'full' | 'executive' | 'custom';
}
```

### Agent Progress Theater (Task 3)
```typescript
// Three-Agent Dashboard (from Story 2.2)
interface AgentProgressProps {
  agents: {
    coordinator: AgentStatus;
    researcher: AgentStatus;
    detective: AgentStatus;
  };
  requestId: string;
}

interface AgentStatus {
  name: string;
  stage: string;
  message: string;
  confidence?: number;
  estimatedTimeRemaining?: number;
  dataSourcesActive: string[];
  insightsDiscovered: number;
}
```

### Dossier Viewer (Task 4)
```typescript
// CIA-Style Dossier Component (from Story 2.2)
interface DossierViewerProps {
  dossier: IntelligenceDossier;
  onSectionToggle: (sectionId: string) => void;
  onExport: () => void;
}

interface IntelligenceDossier {
  companyName: string;
  confidenceScore: number;
  sourceCount: number;
  classification: string;
  sections: IntelligenceSection[];
  dataSources: DataSource[];
}
```

## Testing

### Unit Testing Requirements
- React component rendering and user interactions
- API client methods and error handling
- WebSocket connection management
- Authentication flow and JWT token handling

### Integration Testing Requirements
- End-to-end user flows from login to dossier generation
- Real-time WebSocket updates during agent progress
- API integration with existing backend endpoints
- Mobile responsiveness across different screen sizes

### Performance Testing Requirements
- Frontend bundle size optimization
- WebSocket connection efficiency under load
- Component rendering performance with large dossiers
- API request caching and optimization

## Risk Assessment

**Primary Risk:** Frontend-backend integration complexity with WebSocket real-time updates  
**Mitigation:** Use existing API interfaces exactly as defined in Story 1.2, test integration early  
**Rollback:** Frontend is independent addition - can be disabled without affecting backend

**Compatibility Verification:**
- [x] No breaking changes to existing APIs (frontend is pure consumer)
- [x] Database changes not required (uses existing schema)
- [x] UI follows existing Story 2.2 design patterns
- [x] No performance impact on backend (stateless frontend)

